1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,430
Cycling to work is good for your
health, your wallet and your city.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:07,240
A short ride every morning wakes up your
body and clears your mind before the day

3
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:07,920
begins.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,920
You skip the traffic jams, you never
search for parking and you spend almost

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,080
nothing on fuel.

6
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:16,950
Start with a simple, comfortable
bicycle and a helmet that fits well.

7
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,380
Plan a route on quieter streets or bike
lanes and try it once on a weekend before

8
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,730
your first working day.

9
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,720
Carry a small bag with a spare
tube, a pump and a rain jacket.

10
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,780
Use lights at the front and back when it
gets dark and always signal before you

11
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:31,310
turn.

12
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,460
If your office is far away, ride to
a train or bus station and finish the

13
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,280
journey there.

14
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:40,680
After a few weeks, the ride will feel
easy and you may even look forward to it.

15
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,200
Fewer cars on the road also
means cleaner air for everyone.

16
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,000
Many cities now add new bike lanes every
year so the ride keeps getting safer.

17
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,060
Check your tires and brakes once a month
and your bicycle will serve you well for

18
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:53,720
years.
